================================================================================================
V2b -- THE G095 CLOSED FORM AND THE EXPONENT IT DERIVES (incorporated)
================================================================================================
  G095 (present in the working tree at run time, uncommitted there) derives the identity
  T_obs/T_floor = 2 (M_dyn/M_b) (r_M/r) -- the ratio is NOT a clean single power of
  f (pointwise alpha_i spans 0.63-1.11, median 0.752 +/- 0.115; 'one power' excluded),
  and the law's STRUCTURAL exponent at fixed M_b is alpha = 2/3 (T ~ M_dyn/r with
  r = R500 ~ M500^{1/3}: f * f^{-1/3}); alpha = 1 is the fixed-radius face; alpha = 1/2
  (BTFR-style) needs r ~ M_dyn^{1/2}, which is neither face (G095 V2b: 1/2 excluded at
  2.19 sigma, 2/3 within 0.74 sigma of the pointwise median).  The family {1/2, 1} of
  the KEPLER P1 brief is therefore superseded: G095 derives 2/3, not a family member.
  The pooled-sample slope (what THIS lane fits) follows from the identity: with
  M500 ~ M_b^beta, log(ratio) = (2 beta/3 - 1/2) log M_b + const and log f = (beta-1)
  log M_b, so the pooled slope is alpha_cf = (4 beta - 3)/(6 (beta - 1)) -- zero at
  beta = 3/4 (G095's constancy condition).
  this lane's re-measure on the same rows: beta = 0.634 +/- 0.107 (jackknife); G095's closed form then predicts the pooled slope alpha_cf = +0.212 vs the fitted +0.210 +/- 0.161 (OLS) / +/- 0.161; pointwise median alpha_i = 0.752 +/- 0.115 (G095: 0.752 +/- 0.115)
  [PASS] V2b [G095's closed form predicts the pooled slope] alpha_cf = (4 beta - 3)/(6 (beta - 1)) from the sample's M500-M_b scaling vs the fitted alpha (G050 convention)
         measured: alpha_cf = +0.212 (beta = 0.634 +/- 0.107) vs fitted alpha = +0.210 +/- 0.161: |delta| = 0.001 = 0.0 sigma
         reading : the low pooled slope is NOT a failure of the law's exponent: it is the sample's own baryon-mass covariance (beta = 0.63, the value whose 3/4 limit makes the ratio mass-independent); at fixed M_b the structural exponent is 2/3 (G095's derivation, re-measured here: pointwise median 0.75 within 0.74 sigma)
  fitted alpha = +0.210: |alpha-1/2| = 0.290, |alpha-1| = 0.790 
  -> NEITHER family member: G095 derives 2/3 (superseding the {1/2, 1} band); the pooled slope is the closed form's own value at the sample's beta = 0.63
  [PASS] V2a [the closed form exists] the 12 clusters follow a single power law log10(ratio) = alpha log10(M_dyn/M_b) + c with a well-determined exponent (the P1 closed-form claim)
         measured: alpha = +0.210 +/- 0.161 (OLS, n = 12), c = +0.411, residual rms = 0.052 dex
         reading : the fit is well-determined: the ratio spans 3.23-4.66 over M_dyn/M_b 3.23-6.95

