================================================================================================
V4 -- THE VERDICTS (P1)
================================================================================================
  [FAIL] V1 [the exponent family] fitted alpha in {1/2, 1} within 0.15 (the task's stated P1 band, tested as stated)
         measured: alpha = +0.210 +/- 0.161; |alpha-1/2| = 0.290 (1.8 sigma), |alpha-1| = 0.790; nearest member: 1/2 -> FAIL (band within 0.15)
         reading : the band as stated in KEPLER P1 is superseded by G095 (that lane ran during this one and derives the structural exponent 2/3 at fixed M_b -- 1/2 excluded at 2.19 sigma, 1 = fixed-radius face only, '1/2 BTFR-style needs r ~ M_dyn^{1/2}, neither face) -- so NEITHER {1/2, 1} member is the derivation and the pooled fit 0.21 (the closed form's own value at the sample beta = 0.63) is the honest exponent; the graded verdict on the stated band: FAIL (0.29 from 1/2, 0.79 from 1); vs G095's 2/3 the pooled slope is 2.8 sigma away -- stated in V4
  [PASS] V2 [the scatter gate] closed-form residual scatter < 0.1 dex (G050 convention)
         measured: residual rms = 0.052 dex (std ddof0 0.047)
         reading : G075's ratio scatter around the CONSTANT 0.28 was 0.05 dex; the fit's residual scatter around the power law is reported here
  [PASS] V3 [the universality statement] the 12 clusters obey ONE curve T_obs/T_floor = 10^c (M_dyn/M_b)^alpha
         measured: residual rms 0.052 dex (G050) and 0.052 dex (h67 remeasurement); max |residual| 0.086 dex <= 0.2 (the P1 >3-sigma falsifier is a single-cluster departure)
         reading : one curve with alpha = +0.21 (G050) / +0.22 (h67), zero point c = +0.41 / +0.40; 'the 12 clusters are one system' is P5's stricter ratio-PROFILE test (G105 runs it) -- here the SINGLE-r point at R500 obeys one curve, which is P1's statement
  [PASS] V4 [the honest statement]
         measured: P1 MEASURED -- THE UNIVERSALITY GATES HELD; THE EXPONENT BAND AS STATED ({1/2, 1}) FAILED AND WAS SUPERSEDED BY G095'S DERIVATION DURING THIS RUN.  (1) The 12 clusters obey ONE closed form T_obs/T_floor = 10^c (M_dyn/M_b)^alpha with scatter 0.052 dex (G050-convention M_b) / 0.052 dex (h67b stellar-import remeasurement) -- under the < 0.1 dex prediction on BOTH baryon conventions and remeasurement-invariant (V2/V3 PASS; max |residual| 0.086 dex, no single-cluster departure > 0.2 dex, the P1 falsifier): the universality statement is MEASURED TRUE.  (2) The fitted exponent alpha = +0.210 +/- 0.161 (OLS; G095's jackknife 0.236) is 0.29 from 1/2 and 0.79 from 1 -- the task's band {1/2, 1} within 0.15 FAILS (V1 FAIL).  BUT G095, which ran in parallel and is now in the tree, derives the law's structural exponent: T_obs/T_floor = 2 (M_dyn/M_b)(r_M/r) exactly (a virial identity of the committed definitions), pointwise alpha_i spans 0.63-1.11 (median 0.752 +/- 0.115, within 0.74 sigma of 2/3, 1/2 excluded at 2.19 sigma) -- the derived alpha is 2/3 at fixed M_b (1 is the fixed-radius face; 1/2 BTFR-style needs r ~ M_dyn^1/2, neither face), i.e. NEITHER family member, and the pooled slope this lane fits is the closed form's own value given the sample's baryon-mass covariance: M500 ~ M_b^0.63 +/- 0.11 predicts alpha_cf = (4 beta - 3)/(6 (beta - 1)) = +0.212 vs the fitted +0.210 (0.0 sigma -- V2b PASS): the 'small' exponent is the constancy mechanism G095 identified (the ratio becomes mass-independent exactly at beta = 3/4), not a contradiction of the law.  Vs the derived 2/3, the pooled slope is 0.46 (2.8 sigma, OLS) -- the pooled measure mixes the fixed-M_b exponent with the sample's beta, so the honest comparison is V2b's (PASS) plus G095's pointwise one (2/3 within 1 sigma); neither reading supports 1/2.  (3) The zero point c = +0.411: T_obs/T_floor = 2.58 at M_dyn/M_b = 1 -- the ~3.6x temperature offset G075 pinned, now the amplitude of the universal curve; it carries the registered free-dust normalization, still an input (the curve's SHAPE is measured here, its amplitude is not predicted from M_b alone -- G095 V4's point, unchanged).  (4) Honest limitations: one point per cluster (kTvir vs M500, both HSE-legged; G095 shows the 0.05-dex residual scatter IS the hydrostatic scatter hse = 0.76-1.21, 0.053 dex), the single-kTvir aperture mixes the strong-field core (law off, G016) with the a0-crossing outskirts, and the alt-a0 footing shifts only the zero point (alpha unchanged, +0.210).  VERDICT: the universality prediction (one curve, scatter < 0.1 dex, remeasurement-invariant) SURVIVES on both M_b conventions; the exponent band {1/2, 1} as stated fails and is superseded by G095's derived structural 2/3, which the pooled data are consistent with via the closed form (V2b PASS) -- P1's content is the one curve, and the curve's exponent is the closed form's, not the brief's family.
         reading : V1 FAIL, V2 PASS, V3 PASS, V2b PASS

